Authors that treat edrioblastoids as the order Edrioblastoida include the Astrocystitidae as the only family of that order,<ref>{{harvnb|Smith|Jell|1990}}</ref> or omit the family level classification as superfluous.<ref>{{harvnb|Zhu|Zamora|Lefebvre|2014}}</ref><ref>{{harvnb|Jell|Sprinke|2021}}</ref>  Authors that treat edrioblastoids as the suborder Edrioblastoidina within the order Edrioasterida include the cyathocystids and rhenopyrgids as either one or two additional families in the suborder.<ref>{{harvnb|Guensburg|Sprinkle|1994}}</ref><ref>{{harvnb|Sprinkle|Sumrall|2015}}</ref>


They have traditionally been the only family in the group, and some who treat edrioblastoids as the order Edrioblastoida omit Aristocystitidae as synonymous with the order.<ref>{{harvnb|Jell|Sprinkle|2021}}</ref>  Those who instead treat edrioblastoids as the suborder Edrioblastoidina within the order Edrioasterida aslo include the cyathocystids and rhenopyrgids in the suborder.<ref>{{harvnb|Guensburg|Sprinkle|1994}}</ref>

