For much of its history, the Astrocystitidae were the only family of edrioblastoids, which were treated either as a class (Edrioblastoidea) or as an edrioasteroid order (Edrioblastoida).  While the family was regularly included for decades, some recent papers have omitted it as redundant, leading to ``Poroblastus`` and ``Ikerus`` being assigned directly to Edrioblastoida.

However, other researchers treat edrioblastoids as the suborder Edrioblastoidina within the order Edrioasterida, and include the cyathocystids and rhenopyrgids as either one or two additional families.  ``Poroblastus`` and ``Ikerus`` are included in the Astrocystitidae as their placement directly under Edrioblastoida is due to Astrocystitidae effectively being a synonym in that classification.

