Historically, the Astrocystitidae were the only family within the class Edrioblastoidea, and contained only the genus ``Astrocystites``.  In 1990, Smith and Jell demoted Edrioblastoidea to the order Edrioblastoida within the Edrioasteroidea, adding the newly described genus ``Cambroblastus`` to the Astrocystitidae but retaining that family as the order's only contents.  In 1994, Guensburg and Sprinkle further demoted the order to the suborder Edrioblastoidina, retaining Astrocystitidae (to which the newly described ''Lampteroblastus'' was added) but also including the cyathocystids and rhenopyrgids as a distinct family.

Later publications treating edrioblastoids as an order continue to place only the Astrocystitidae within it, but in some cases the family is omitted as redundant.  The genera ``Poroblastus`` and ``Ikerus`` were assigned directly to the order Edrioblastoida in this manner, but are included here to ensure the correct definition of Astrocystitidae as it is used within the suborder Edrioblastoidina.



Determining the contents of the Astrocystitidae is slightly complicated due to its omission from some recent descriptions that treat the order Edrioblastoida as essentially synonymoous.  However, researchers that treat the edrioblastoids as the suborder Edrioblastoidina retain the family, as the suborder also contains the cyathocystids and rhenopyrgids.




